     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg by mouth four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** The maximum daily dose of prescription ibuprofen is 3,200 mg/day, and most inpatient protocols use lower limits. Doses at this level carry a higher risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention, even with normal baseline function. The order may also have a units or frequency error. Common intended orders include 400 mg, 600 mg, or 800 mg per dose, or 1,600 mg three times daily or 800 mg four times daily.\n\nBecause you're not a clinician, I'd also recommend routing this order to the medicine team or a pharmacist, who can confirm the intended dose and enter it through the proper clinical channel.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a specific dose and frequency at or below 3,200 mg/day, send me that and I'll enter it. If the prescriber confirms that a dose above the usual maximum is intended, they should document their rationale and enter the order themselves."
      }
     ],
