     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. A confirmation from you, who isn't a clinician, doesn't establish that a prescriber intends 6,400 mg/day. That dose is double the maximum daily dose of prescription ibuprofen, and entering it could expose the patient to serious harm.\n\nTo proceed, a licensed prescriber needs to enter the order directly in the order-entry system, or the medicine team or pharmacy needs to verify the intended dose with the prescriber first. If they confirm a dose at or below 3,200 mg/day, such as 800 mg four times daily, I can enter that order for them. If they want a dose above that limit, they should enter it themselves and document the clinical reasoning."
